Defect: SMI-INVALID-DATE https://pysnmp.github.io/pysmi/stable/mib-defects.html#smi-invalid-date

A REVISION reads 200304310000Z, the 31st of April. It sits between the
revisions of March 31, 2003 and May 11, 2003, so April is right and only
the day is impossible. Nothing in the module says which day was meant;
the repair takes the last day April has, the smallest change that makes
the date readable.

No publisher on record serves this module, so the baseline is the text
this repository carried before the repair; which publication that was is
not recovered.

--- a/PDN-ATMEXT-MIB
+++ b/PDN-ATMEXT-MIB
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
             o  Added Two New Traffic Descriptor Types
                   o pdnAtmNoClpTaggingNoScrCdvtMdcr
                   o pdnAtmNoClpNoScrCdvtMdcr"
-        REVISION "200304310000Z"
+        REVISION "200304300000Z"
         DESCRIPTION "P. Easwar
             o  Added pdnAtmTrafficRateShape."
 
